<title>HONDURAS: Honduras plans to cut raw material import duty.</title>
<headline>Honduras plans to cut raw material import duty.</headline>
<dateline>TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honduras may slash its tariff on imported raw materials to one percent from five percent in an effort to help exporters, an official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The administration of President Carlos Roberto Reina sent a bill proposing the tariff cut to Congress, where it is expected to pass easily, congressional spokesman Gustavo Alfaro said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is necessary to cut the tax on raw material imports to allow our export industry to compete with the rest of Central America,&quot; Alfaro said.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Palencia, Honduras bureau +504 31-53-29))</p>
